                    {
                        "sense_id": "25507b1c-baef-37b9-8294-ed614eb3c5dc",
                        "entry_id": "be2cc60e-c640-30f3-9d1b-7e232817ea3a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui se développe entre les pôles, en parlant d’un champ magnétique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "physical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "50426be2-8d41-4bb7-9d79-6a67d4a824c3",
                                "sense_id": "25507b1c-baef-37b9-8294-ed614eb3c5dc",
                                "text": "Dans l’autre cas, la topologie des lignes de champ poloïdal change."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f5fe602f-27da-3ec5-8e46-46d213903641",
                        "entry_id": "be2cc60e-c640-30f3-9d1b-7e232817ea3a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui a la forme d’une poloïde, par exemple le champ poloïdal dans un tokamak."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0193871a-12c6-4b41-91d1-a58021dde23a",
                        "source_entry_id": "be2cc60e-c640-30f3-9d1b-7e232817ea3a",
                        "target_lang_word": "poloidal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "poloidal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa3e4dad-4be6-38dd-ab78-d20c3cae25aa",
                                        "entry_id": "a4e02f5e-40b8-31f0-80c0-3c68d4323e99",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, pertaining to, or shaped like a poloid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ca52512-bc6f-4ac2-a802-812fcc8684b5",
                                                "sense_id": "fa3e4dad-4be6-38dd-ab78-d20c3cae25aa",
                                                "text": "Two different pathways, called poloids, are obtained depending on whether A is considered as the fixed frame, or whether B is considered as the fixed frame. The two poloidal curves roll on each other, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2714d9a0-0906-31b3-8a39-61b3b8b48b7f",
                                        "entry_id": "a4e02f5e-40b8-31f0-80c0-3c68d4323e99",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Between the poles of a magnet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a2940e9-3f82-410b-bd20-cb27e2582ee4",
                                                "sense_id": "2714d9a0-0906-31b3-8a39-61b3b8b48b7f",
                                                "text": "A poloidal magnetic field has closed field lines that begin and end on fictitious “poles,\" as in the case of a bar magnet or William Gilbert's lodestone."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "48978e0a-7abf-32ed-9c53-ad64f03671b2",
                                        "entry_id": "a4e02f5e-40b8-31f0-80c0-3c68d4323e99",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a direction on a torus perpendicular to a line that traces around the outside of a torus, or on a sphere perpendicular to the equator, going through both poles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4219bab6-99dd-48bc-8ca9-7485e11cdc47",
                                                "sense_id": "48978e0a-7abf-32ed-9c53-ad64f03671b2",
                                                "text": "The magnetic field can be written as the sum of a poloidal field and a toroidal field, and many of the concepts of dynamo theory revolve around the question of how to generate a toroidal field from a poloidal field and, conversely, how to generate a poloidal field from a toroidal field."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77ba07cf-c654-44d5-8d6b-426a7d38dd25",
                                                "sense_id": "48978e0a-7abf-32ed-9c53-ad64f03671b2",
                                                "text": "While the slope of the toroidal velocity distribution at the outer surface is generally in good agreement with the observed surface value, poloidal velocity consistently shows reduced energy at low harmonics ."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
